functor: 1
title: rot
---

set heading(numbering: none)

`rot` · reflect · the same thing in a new direction, such as an arrow up.

# Form

`x.rot` on a symbol, `(a + b).rot` on a group. A recipe has one base and up to three operations.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | The same thing in a new direction, such as an arrow up. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | Use a `sym` to give a recipe a short name. |
| Construction | A mirror image or a half turn of the base. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- More than three operations on one base gives a warning.

# From LaTeX

no LaTeX command.

